le, the south entrance off 90th street, provides users access to 4 miles of hiking trails, 14 miles of single track mountain bike trails, an access to Bertram Lake and  a carry-in access to Long Lake which will allow users the opportunity to paddle Long, Mud and First Lakes.  If you are riding the mountain bike trails, this is where you will want to park.\n\nThe main park entrance is located at 9842 Briarwood Avenue NE, Monticello MN on the North end of Bertram Lake, this entrance provides users access to the swimming beach, hiking trials, picnic facilities, picnic shelter (available for reservation), and a four season climate controlled chalet, and Camp Manitou facilities/day camp.","amenities":[],"waiverUrl":null,"url":"https://www.wrightcountymn.gov/Facilities/Facility/Details/Bertram-Chain-of-Lakes-Regional-Park-52","socials":{"Facebook":"BertramSingletrack","Trailforks":"https://www.trailforks.com/region/bertram-chain-of-lakes-13707/","MTB Project":"https://www.mtbproject.com/trail/3505586/bertram-chain-of-lakes"},"maps":{"Trails (PDF)":"https://www.wrightcountymn.gov/DocumentCenter/View/15145/Bertram-Park-Map?bidId="},"agency":"Wright County","statusTags":[],"organizationId":"OUrkWOo2IydWZaG1Hy81","organization":{"name":"Minnesota Off-Road Cyclists","shortName":"MORC","url":"https://www.morcmtb.org/","logoUrl":"https://storage.googleapis.com/trailbot-covers-prod/6b99e26e-c135-4de4-adc9-54eda2e46476.jpg","slug":"morc","flags":["volunteers","donations","memberships"],"embedKey":"36dc2fd4-babb-4355-bd81-0722b7c84838","timezone":"America/Chicago"},"street":"1744 90th Street NE","embedKey":"7861a68c-f28e-4435-8585-9e3451acf72d","latestUpdateId":"Uh4Jh_lL07cVMqjSX-_cn","defaults":{"hideOsmTrails":false},"fields":{},"customFields":{},"last24Precip":0.2,"last24PrecipType":"rain","regions":["Twin Cities Metro"]},{"trailId":"dbef1a89-e0a9-46fb-94a6-4eb68b4aec0a","trailName":"Monarch Singletrack","description":"","trailStatus":"Closed","city":"Waconia","state":"MN","country":"US","lat":44.8779294,"long":-93.7192217,"zipcode":"55387","timezone":"America/Chicago","pictures":[],"active":true,"visibility":"public","updatedAt":1790439660449,"slug":"monarch-singletrack","logoUrl":null,"coverUrl":null,"joinUrl":"https://www.morcmtb.org/store","donationUrl":"https://www.morcmtb.org/store","ticketUrl":null,"volunteerUrl":"https://www.morcmtb.org/monarch","sourceDescription":"Updates are provided directly by trail maintainers.","ebikePolicy":null,"weatherPolicy":null,"notes":"Open 5am-10pm. Test your skills and get your adrenaline going on Three Rivers' newest mountain bike trail. Nestled on the western edge of the park, the Monarch Singletrack at Carver Park Reserve has over 10 miles of trails ranging from easy to advanced, including a trail built with adapted cycles in mind. The trail is also open to hikers and snowshoers and can be accessed from two locations: Springview Drive year-round and Grimm Road in the summer and fall. \n\nExplore the park’s wetlands, grasslands and woodlands on one of five trail loops within the singletrack. For beginners and adapted cyclists, wider trails offer gentler rides and a lift and tilt section. More experienced riders can find rocky terrain, bridge crossings, steep drops and long, sustained climbs.","amenities":[],"waiverUrl":null,"url":"https://www.threeriversparks.org/location/monarch-singletrack-trail","socials":{"Facebook":"monarchsingletrack","Trailforks":"https://www.trailforks.com/region/carver-park-reserve-41480/"},"maps":{"Trails (Winter)":"https://threeriversparks.link/Carver_ParkReserve_SingletrackTrail_Winter","Trails (Paradise)":"https://threeriversparks.link/Carver_ParkReserve_SingletrackTrail_Advanced","Trails (Summer)":"https://threeriversparks.link/Carver_ParkReserve_SingletrackTrail_Summer"},"agency":"Three Rivers Park District","statusTags":["wet"],"organizationId":"OUrkWOo2IydWZaG1Hy81","organization":{"name":"Minnesota Off-Road Cyclists","shortName":"MORC","url":"https://www.morcmtb.org/","logoUrl":"https://storage.googleapis.com/trailbot-covers-prod/6b99e26e-c135-4de4-adc9-54eda2e46476.jpg","slug":"morc","flags":["volunteers","donations","memberships"],"embedKey":"36dc2fd4-babb-4355-bd81-0722b7c84838","timezone":"America/Chicago"},"street":"Monarch Singletrack Trailhead","embedKey":"67ab64a7-0d4e-44ee-99e6-ec588f410be9","latestUpdateId":"CZfWCsWg1AF_zCgXsFH0O","defaults":{"hideOsmTrails":false},"fields":{},"customFields":{},"last24Precip":0.2,"last24PrecipType":"rain","regions":["Twin Cities Metro"]},{"trailId":"31044f9c-d539-4b16-b22f-29ea0a288642","trailName":"Lone Lake Park","description":"The rain has started and looks like it will be falling for several hours. ","trailStatus":"Closed","city":"Minnetonka","state":"MN","country":"US","lat":44.9,"long":-93.43,"zipcode":"55343","timezone":"America/Chicago","pictures":[],"active":true,"visibility":"public","updatedAt":1790437209670,"slug":"lone-lake-park","logoUrl":"https://storage.googleapis.com/trailbot-covers-prod/87435bf9-a42d-49ae-a17a-72bd66b2ed39.jpg","coverUrl":"https://storage.googleapis.com/trailbot-covers-prod/ff582bb3-d2a9-45d7-835c-e19f2e4ec5c4.jpeg","joinUrl":"https://www.morcmtb.org/store","donationUrl":"https://www.morcmtb.org/store/","ticketUrl":null,"volunteerUrl":"https://www.signupgenius.com/go/9040945aba82cabfa7-park1#/","sourceDescription":"Updates are provided directly by trail maintainers.","ebikePolicy":null,"weatherPolicy":"Do not use the trail when it’s raining or you are leaving tracks in the trail tread.","notes":"Lone Lake Park's 5-mile, multi-use mountain bike trail entices riders, hikers and snowshoers to experience the fun and natural beauty of Minnetonka's Big Woods representative forest.\n\nTwo trailheads provide users easy access from Rowland Road, in the park's southwest section, or Shady Oak Road in the east. We encourage riders to leave their cars at home and access the park from one of our great bike trails, including the Minnesota River Bluffs LRT.\n\nLone Lake Park is designed to accommodate a variety of mountain biking skill levels, and the trail offers ample challenges, from the steep topography to the fast, flowy single-track.","amenities":[],"waiverUrl":null,"url":"https://www.minnetonkamn.gov/our-city/parks-and-trails/trails/lone-lake-park-mountain-bike-trail","socials":{"Facebook":"MinnetonkaMTB","Trailforks":"https://www.trailforks.com/region/lone-lake-park-42675/","MTB Project":"https://www.mtbproject.com/trail/7055967/multi-use-mountain-bike-trail"},"maps":{"Trails (PDF)":"https://www.minnetonkamn.gov/home/showpublisheddocument?id=8411","Trails (Interactive)":"https://mtka.maps.arcgis.com/apps/webappviewer/index.html?id=e17e9d2d953c49a2a7e08088964a2fe4"},"agency":"City of Minnetonka, MN","statusTags":["wet"],"organizationId":"OUrkWOo2IydWZaG1Hy81","organization":{"name":"Minnesota Off-Road Cyclists","shortName":"MORC","url":"https://www.morcmtb.org/","logoUrl":"https://storage.googleapis.com/trailbot-covers-prod/6b99e26e-c135-4de4-adc9-54eda2e46476.jpg","slug":"morc","flags":["volunteers","donations","memberships"],"embedKey":"36dc2fd4-babb-4355-bd81-0722b7c84838","timezone":"America/Chicago"},"street":" 5624 Shady Oak Rd","embedKey":"353962eb-02a8-40b3-8f97-820fe63d5efb","latestUpdateId":"OuYsLKWIcbIdn2nvpGbU2","defaults":{"hideOsmTrails":false},"fields":{},"customFields":{},"last24Precip":0.1,"last24PrecipType":"rain","regions":["Twin Cities Metro"]},{"trailId":"3b716fa1-af6b-4aa8-aff1-11ff473072d1","trailName":"Battle Creek","description":" there’s a report of a dead deer on Ferngully. We’ve notified Ramsey County, but don’t have timeline for clearing it out. 🥲\n\nalso a few trees down one on dingo and a few on Travis so take caution","trailStatus":"Open","city":"St Paul","state":"MN","country":"US","lat":44.936068,"long":-93.0216788,"zipcode":"55119","timezone":"America/Chicago","pictures":[],"active":true,"visibility":"public","updatedAt":1790291247273,"slug":"battle-creek","logoUrl":null,"coverUrl":null,"joinUrl":"https://www.morcmtb.org/store","donationUrl":"https://www.morcmtb.org/store","ticketUrl":null,"volunteerUrl":"https://www.morcmtb.org/battle-creek","sourceDescription":"Updates are provided directly by trail maintainers.","ebikePolicy":null,"weatherPolicy":null,"notes":"Store to purchase Battle Creek swag! https://lifebrand.co/store/brand/my-brand/battle-creek-mtb-st-paul/\n\nBattle Creek Rec Center Trailhead (75 Winthrop St S). Quickest way to the singletrack is up the hill South of the Rec Center.  Follow the looping Cat Walk trail up to the entrance of the Higher Ed singletrack. \n\nAnother trail entrance is on Battle Creek Road between Upper Afton Rd and Lower Afton Rd.  Look for the singletrack signs, and there's usually cars parked nearby.  From here you can access the trails above the Rec Center, and also the trails along the bluff (like Wall of Death) and get access to the Overlook trail. \n\n(Note: there is another parking lot available off Pt. Douglas Road - we don't recommend using it, as there have been quite a few break-ins at the Pt. Douglas lot.)\n\nBattle Creek offers quite an extensive network of trails, as compared to most metropolitan trail systems. In many areas of the park, it's easy to forget you're surrounded by suburbs on all sides. Battle Creek has something for riders of all technical abilities, with trails running the gamut from smooth, hard-pack ski trails to expert-level singletrack. The terrain is quite hilly, so expect the trails to give you a good workout. Although hilly, the climbs tend to be relatively short, with the longest single climb gaining approximately 110' in elevation. Trails are mainly fast hardpack, with a few sandy sections and a few rocks & roots.","amenities":[],"waiverUrl":null,"url":"https://www.ramseycounty.us/residents/parks-recreation/parks-trails/trails/mountain-biking-trails","socials":{"Facebook":"battlecreekmountainbike","Trailforks":"https://www.trailforks.com/region/battle-creek-5538/","MTB Project":"https://www.mtbproject.com/directory/8013784/battle-creek-regional-park"},"maps":{"Trails (PDF)":"https://assets.ramseycountymn.gov/files/migrated-files/2017_Battle_Creek_Off_Road_Cycling_Draft_Map.pdf"},"agency":"Ramsey County","statusTags":["caution"],"organizationId":"OUrkWOo2IydWZaG1Hy81","organization":{"name":"Minnesota Off-Road Cyclists","shortName":"MORC","url":"https://www.morcmtb.org/","logoUrl":"https://storage.googleapis.com/trailbot-covers-prod/6b99e26e-c135-4de4-adc9-54eda2e46476.jpg","slug":"morc","flags":["volunteers","donations","memberships"],"embedKey":"36dc2fd4-babb-4355-bd81-0722b7c84838","timezone":"America/Chicago"},"street":"Battle Creek Rd","embedKey":"08db40fd-7459-4468-8017-dab108fa4641","latestUpdateId":"qjBY7VzjG6ibCU81_kLci","defaults":{"hideOsmTrails":false},"fields":{},"customFields":{},"last24Precip":0.1,"last24PrecipType":"rain","regions":["Twin Cities Metro"]},{"trailId":"10e3fba6-063b-46af-a1af-22184be83cd1","trailName":"Lake Rebecca","description":"Rain coming through. Gates CLOSED. Thanks!","trailStatus":"Closed","city":"Rockford","state":"MN","country":"US","lat":45.0717787,"long":-93.7589576,"zipcode":"55373","timezone":"America/Chicago","pictures":[],"active":true,"visibility":"public","updatedAt":1790281146704,"slug":"lake-rebecca","logoUrl":null,"coverUrl":null,"joinUrl":"https://www.morcmtb.org/store","donationUrl":"https://www.morcmtb.org/store","ticketUrl":null,"volunteerUrl":"https://www.morcmtb.org/lake-rebecca","sourceDescription":"Updates are provided directly by trail maintainers.","ebikePolicy":null,"weatherPolicy":"During the summer, the trail typically needs 24 hours to dry out after a rain event of .2\" or greater.  Humidity and low temperatures could cause it to take longer to dry out.","notes":"Open 5am-10pm. A gently rolling Big Woods landscape and numerous wetland areas make up the beautiful Lake Rebecca Park Reserve. In addition to the many opportunities for outdoor fun you'll find here, this park is also a haven for wildlife, including trumpeter swans.","amenities":[],"waiverUrl":null,"url":"https://www.threeriversparks.org/location/lake-rebecca-singletrack-trail","socials":{"Trailforks":"https://www.trailforks.com/region/lake-rebecca-12004/","MTB Project":"https://www.mtbproject.com/trail/7024093/lake-rebecca-loop","Facebook":"LakeRebeccaSingletrack"},"maps":{"Winter (PDF)":"https://threeriversparks.link/LakeRebecca_ParkReserve_Winter","Singletrack (PDF)":"https://threeriversparks.link/LakeRebecca_ParkReserve_SingletrackTrail","Interactive":"https://www.threeriversparks.org/location/lake-rebecca-park-reserve","Summer (PDF)":"https://threeriversparks.link/LakeRebecca_ParkReserve_Summer","Singletrack (Avenza)":"https://www.avenzamaps.com/maps/1208834/lake-rebecca-park-reserve-singletrack-trail"},"agency":"Three Rivers Park District","statusTags":["greasy","wet"],"organizationId":"OUrkWOo2IydWZaG1Hy81","organization":{"name":"Minnesota Off-Road Cyclists","shortName":"MORC","url":"https://www.morcmtb.org/","logoUrl":"https://storage.googleapis.com/trailbot-covers-prod/6b99e26e-c135-4de4-adc9-54eda2e46476.jpg","slug":"morc","flags":["volunteers","donations","memberships"],"embedKey":"36dc2fd4-babb-4355-bd81-0722b7c84838","timezone":"America/Chicago"},"street":"9831 Rebecca Park Trail","embedKey":"e0b2f114-3533-435a-979e-0ef28e274622","latestUpdateId":"ARbTVrzE2MbOFAw_avpwW","defaults":{"hideOsmTrails":false},"fields":{},"customFields":{},"last24Precip":0.2,"last24PrecipType":"rain","regions":["Twin Cities Metro"]},{"trailId":"4c82f3f0-9f45-4e16-a436-f490fbea81a4","trailName":"Theodore Wirth: MOCA/MORC Trails","description":"\n\nHeads-up Theo Peeps…..\n\nThis Friday, September 25th from 4:30pm until done, the MOCA/MORC Trail Crew will be raining destruction with pointy tools on the the north exit of the South West Wirth section to prepare it to be enhanced by the contractor repaving the adjacent paved bike trail. The exit will be torn up for several days until the contractor can complete their work. The goal of this effort is to reduce the amount of gravel that makes its way out onto the paved trail as a result of Skiddy McSkiddingtons getting their skidding thing on as they depart the section. \n\nDuring this disruption, please expect that you may need to carry your bike across the construction area to reduce the likelihood of fall down go boom. \n\nWe know. Now you do too. \n\nTheo for Theo\n\nShout if you have any questions.","trailStatus":"Open","city":"Minneapolis","state":"MN","country":"US","lat":44.9923964,"long":-93.325502,"zipcode":"55422","timezone":"America/Chicago","pictures":["https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/trail-updates-pictures/o/fd7db293-4bb2-4d8c-8902-2730cbb3823b.jpg?alt=media"],"active":true,"visibility":"public","updatedAt":1790269263943,"slug":"theodore-wirth-moca-morc-trails","logoUrl":null,"coverUrl":null,"joinUrl":null,"donationUrl":"https://www.morcmtb.org/store","ticketUrl":null,"volunteerUrl":null,"sourceDescription":"Updates are provided directly by trail maintainers.","ebikePolicy":"Class 1 Pedal Assist ONLY!","weatherPolicy":"Trails are closed when wet. Gates are for extended closure.  A closed gate always means a closed trail or trail section. An open gate does NOT mean an open trail or trail section. Always check Trailbot for official conditions before heading to the land of Theo.","notes":"The mountain bike trails at Theo are managed by two different organizations, the Loppet Foundation and Minneapolis Off-Road Cycling Advocates (MOCA/MORC). MOCA manages North Loop, South Loop, Glenwood, Southwest Wirth, and Brownie Trails.","amenities":[],"waiverUrl":null,"url":"https://www.minneapolisparks.org/parks__destinations/trails__parkways/off-road_cycling_trails/","socials":{"Facebook":"theowirthsingletrack","Trailforks":"https://www.trailforks.com/region/theodore-wirth-park/","MTB Project":"https://www.mtbproject.com/directory/8014425/theodore-wirth-park"},"maps":{"South Loop":"htt