"volunteerUrl":"https://www.morcmtb.org/","sourceDescription":"Updates are provided directly by trail maintainers.","ebikePolicy":"Operating e-motos on any Three Rivers Park District trail is prohibited. This includes both paved and unpaved regional trails as well as singletrack mountain bike trails.\n\nE-motos are electric-powered two-wheeled off-highway vehicles (OHVs) that resemble dirt bikes. They often lack pedals, rely on a throttle for acceleration and can reach speeds greater than 28 mph.\n\nSome e-motos may include pedals and look similar to e-bikes but they travel at much higher speeds, often include an optional throttle and are not classified as e-bikes.\n\nOther e-motos are designed for road or paved use and are considered electric mopeds or electric motorcycles. These vehicles are subject to state motor vehicle laws and restrictions and are not permitted on any Park District trails.","weatherPolicy":null,"notes":"Open 5am-10pm. With over 10 miles of trail and loops rated from easy to advanced, Murphy-Hanrehan Park Reserve is a favorite spot for mountain biking in the Twin Cities. The singletrack trail gives bikers an amazing off-road experience.","amenities":["changing-area","drinking-water","free-parking","picnic-area","bike-repair-station","restrooms","trail-map","trail-signage","tire-pump"],"waiverUrl":null,"url":"https://www.threeriversparks.org/location/murphy-hanrehan-singletrack-trail","socials":{"Facebook":"MurphyHanrehanSingletrack","Trailforks":"https://www.trailforks.com/region/murphyhanrehan-park/","MTB Project":"https://www.mtbproject.com/trail/3522002/murphy-hanrehan"},"maps":{"Singletrack (Avenza)":"https://www.avenzamaps.com/maps/1208809/murphy-hanrehan-park-reserve-singletrack-trail","Singletrack (PDF)":"https://threeriversparks.link/Murphy-Hanrehan_ParkReserve_SingletrackTrail","Winter (PDF)":"https://threeriversparks.link/Murphy-Hanrehan_ParkReserve_Winter","Summer (PDF)":"https://threeriversparks.link/Murphy-Hanrehan_ParkReserve_Summer","Summer (Avenza)":"https://www.avenzamaps.com/maps/1208859/murphy-hanrehan-park-reserve-summer","Winter (Avenza)":"https://www.avenzamaps.com/maps/1208845/murphy-hanrehan-park-reserve-winter"},"agency":"Scott County / Three Rivers Park District","statusTags":["tacky"],"organizationId":"OUrkWOo2IydWZaG1Hy81","organization":{"name":"Minnesota Off-Road Cyclists","shortName":"MORC","url":"https://www.morcmtb.org/","logoUrl":"https://storage.googleapis.com/trailbot-covers-prod/6b99e26e-c135-4de4-adc9-54eda2e46476.jpg","slug":"morc","flags":["volunteers","donations","memberships"],"embedKey":"36dc2fd4-babb-4355-bd81-0722b7c84838","timezone":"America/Chicago"},"street":"15663 Murphy Lake Blvd","embedKey":"9216d42a-44a0-4780-afba-d17357826297","latestUpdateId":"lH4TuAF9ABf0P1245Q9Xc","defaults":{"hideOsmTrails":false},"fields":{},"customFields":{},"last24Precip":0.2,"last24PrecipType":"rain","regions":["Twin Cities Metro"]},{"trailId":"2cce9ec0-a0aa-41ca-9348-9849803fe7b3","trailName":"Lebanon Hills","description":"Open but rain showers are in the area so don't ride if it turns muddy again. Watch out for slick corners and fallen trees. As usual, report back here on Trailbot with any issues you find.","trailStatus":"Open","city":"Eagan","state":"MN","country":"US","lat":44.7821,"long":-93.1880352,"zipcode":"55122","timezone":"America/Chicago","pictures":[],"active":true,"visibility":"public","updatedAt":1790016217327,"slug":"lebanon-hills","logoUrl":"https://storage.googleapis.com/trailbot-covers-prod/f09e3a4b-28f7-4901-afc6-dde59108fc9a.jpg","coverUrl":"https://storage.googleapis.com/trailbot-covers-prod/9fbc35fa-55bf-4a59-9ae0-77633a4f0370.jpg","joinUrl":"https://www.morcmtb.org/store","donationUrl":"https://www.morcmtb.org/donate","ticketUrl":null,"volunteerUrl":"https://www.morcmtb.org/lebanon-hills","sourceDescription":"Updates are provided directly by trail maintainers.","ebikePolicy":"Electric-assist or pedal-assist bicycles are allowed wherever normal bicycles are allowed as long as they meet the definition in Minnesota Statute 169.011, Subdivision 27. https://www.revisor.mn.gov/statutes/cite/169.011#stat.169.011.27 Please note, more powerful bikes known as e-moto's are NOT allowed and have caused damage to the trail.","weatherPolicy":"The gates will be closed after soaking rainfall events but we leave it up to everyone's best judgement otherwise, regardless of posted condition. Please don't abuse this privilege and ride in muddy conditions. If you are leaving tracks on the trail or picking up mud on your tires, please turn back and ride later instead.","notes":"Lebanon Hills Regional Park has nearly 12 miles of one-way mountain biking singletrack with trails for all skill levels, including a skills park at the trailhead. Features throughout include; berms, jumps, tables, drops, step-ups, log piles, rock gardens, skinny's, and more (with the big stuff being a large rock drop and jump into a ravine). The West Trailhead facilities include; parking, restrooms, drinking fountain / bottle filler, picnic shelter, grills, fire pit, and repair stands. All use of these facilities and mountain bike trails are free, but with respect to the Dakota County Parks rules. For overflow parking, park over on Galaxie Ave. and use the entrance across from Safari Trail road.","amenities":["picnic-area","skills-area","trail-signage","free-parking","bike-repair-station","drinking-water","restrooms","tire-pump","trail-map"],"waiverUrl":null,"url":"https://www.co.dakota.mn.us/parks/parksTrails/LebanonHills","socials":{"Trailforks":"https://www.trailforks.com/region/lebanon-hills/","MTB Project":"https://www.mtbproject.com/directory/8011629/lebanon-hills-regional-park","Facebook":"lebanonhills.mtb"},"maps":{"Central - All Season (PDF)":"https://www.co.dakota.mn.us/parks/Documents/LebanonHillsCentralSummerWinterTrailMap.pdf","Winter (PDF)":"https://www.co.dakota.mn.us/parks/Documents/LebanonHillsWinterTrailMap.pdf","Mountain Biking - All Season (PDF)":"https://www.co.dakota.mn.us/parks/Documents/LebanonHillsWestMtBikeSummerWinterTrailMap.pdf","Summer (PDF)":"https://www.co.dakota.mn.us/parks/Documents/LebanonHillsSummerTrailMap.pdf","Mountain Biking - All Season (Avenza)":"https://www.avenzamaps.com/maps/180061/lebanon-hills-regional-park-west-mt-bike-all-season-sign"},"agency":"Dakota County","statusTags":[],"organizationId":"OUrkWOo2IydWZaG1Hy81","organization":{"name":"Minnesota Off-Road Cyclists","shortName":"MORC","url":"https://www.morcmtb.org/","logoUrl":"https://storage.googleapis.com/trailbot-covers-prod/6b99e26e-c135-4de4-adc9-54eda2e46476.jpg","slug":"morc","flags":["volunteers","donations","memberships"],"embedKey":"36dc2fd4-babb-4355-bd81-0722b7c84838","timezone":"America/Chicago"},"street":"4801 Johnny Cake Ridge Road","embedKey":"10a0e3e7-f819-441a-9453-96f96a766531","latestUpdateId":"T0h9kVJ9532FITZCYY7G2","defaults":{"hideOsmTrails":false},"fields":{},"customFields":{},"last24Precip":0.2,"last24PrecipType":"rain","regions":["Twin Cities Metro"]},{"trailId":"923d48e8-9c9a-465b-b02f-d2823731667d","trailName":"Rice Creek Chain of Lakes","description":"","trailStatus":"Open","city":"Lino Lakes","state":"MN","country":"US","lat":45.1635553,"long":-93.1145047,"zipcode":"55014","timezone":"America/Chicago","pictures":[],"active":true,"visibility":"public","updatedAt":1789936621962,"slug":"rice-creek-chain-of-lakes","logoUrl":null,"coverUrl":null,"joinUrl":null,"donationUrl":"https://www.morcmtb.org/store/","ticketUrl":null,"volunteerUrl":"https://www.morcmtb.org/volunteer/","sourceDescription":"Updates are provided directly by trail maintainers.","ebikePolicy":null,"weatherPolicy":null,"notes":"The Rice Creek Chain of Lakes Park Reserve Single Track Trails consist of two separate trail loops. These trails are entry level (beginner/green)and are suitable for most riders. Both trails are one-way continuous loops that have a single entry/exit point connecting them to an existing paved trail. Riders will use the paved trails to access the new single track trail loops.  - Rice Lake Trail features a few challenging climbs to elevate the heart rate, combined with fun flowing segments at a total length of approximately 1.4 mi. Sherman Lake Trail is also a flowing design, however, will feature a few jump opportunities and a couple down-hill segments that should add a little thrill for the gravity fans. The Sherman Lake Trail is around 1.8 mi. in length.","amenities":[],"waiverUrl":null,"url":"https://www.anokacountyparks.com/things-to-do","socials":{},"maps":{"Google":"https://www.google.com/maps/d/u/0/viewer?ll=45.16809627209439%2C-93.08916599999999&z=14&mid=1MGzrXnfXnlTYw9PLESfFQtbxPKSTmwMP","Sherman Lake Trailhead":"https://www.anokacountyparks.com/s/Sherman-Lake-trailhead.pdf","Rice Lake Trailhead":"https://www.anokacountyparks.com/s/Rice-Lake-Trailhead.pdf"},"agency":"Anoka County ","statusTags":["soft"],"organizationId":"OUrkWOo2IydWZaG1Hy81","organization":{"name":"Minnesota Off-Road Cyclists","shortName":"MORC","url":"https://www.morcmtb.org/","logoUrl":"https://storage.googleapis.com/trailbot-covers-prod/6b99e26e-c135-4de4-adc9-54eda2e46476.jpg","slug":"morc","flags":["volunteers","donations","memberships"],"embedKey":"36dc2fd4-babb-4355-bd81-0722b7c84838","timezone":"America/Chicago"},"street":"623 Aqua Ln","embedKey":"0ab9ff7f-a849-47df-af86-8cba2733557f","latestUpdateId":"Hd0p7W-E0RbnqDMjmMmRi","defaults":{"hideOsmTrails":false},"fields":{},"customFields":{},"last24Precip":0.1,"last24PrecipType":"rain","regions":["Twin Cities Metro"]},{"trailId":"ff41d044-a495-4a11-a9ed-b1e6265377e4","trailName":"Sunfish Lake Park","description":"probably fine, probably a couple puddles ","trailStatus":"Open","city":"Lake Elmo","state":"MN","country":"US","lat":45.0037331,"long":-92.914928,"zipcode":"55042","timezone":"America/Chicago","pictures":[],"active":true,"visibility":"public","updatedAt":1789914459273,"slug":"sunfish-lake-park","logoUrl":null,"coverUrl":null,"joinUrl"